<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Real-world Perfo=
rmance Metrics</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">In my previous fintech applicati=
on, these optimizations achieved:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reduced initial load ti=
me</strong> from 3.2s to 1.8s for 10,000 transactions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Improved scroll perform=
ance</strong> from 15fps to 60fps on mobile devices</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Decreased memory usage<=
/strong> by 40% during long sessions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Reduced time-to-interac=
tive</strong> for complex filtering operations from 800ms to 200ms</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The key insight is that =
Redux performance optimization is about understanding data flow patterns an=
d optimizing for your specific use cases.</strong> Banking applications hav=
e unique characteristics - users often keep sessions open for extended peri=
ods, perform many small transactions, and need immediate feedback for finan=
cial operations.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding! Your approach to performance optimization shows real production =
experience. I'm particularly impressed with your memory management strategy=
 and the optimistic updates pattern - those are exactly the kinds of challe=
nges we face at NAB.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let's shift gears a bit. Redux h=
as been around for a while now, and there are newer state management soluti=
ons emerging. You mentioned Zustand and Jotai in your intro. How do you eva=
luate when to use Redux versus these newer alternatives? And where do you s=
ee state management heading in the React ecosystem?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's an excellent question and something I think about frequently, especially=
 when architecting new projects or recommending migrations. <strong>The sta=
te management landscape has evolved significantly, and the "one-size-fits-a=
ll" approach is becoming less relevant.</strong></p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">My Decision Fram=
ework for State Management</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I use what I call the <strong>"S=
tate Management Decision Tree"</strong> based on several key factors:</p>
