<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key Innovations in This =
Real-time Approach:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Incremental Index Updat=
es</strong>: Never rebuild entire indices, only update affected entries</li=
>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Multiple Index Types</s=
trong>: Time-based, amount-range, category, and status indices for optimal =
query planning</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Adaptive Strategy Selec=
tion</strong>: Automatically choose between indexed and sequential filterin=
g based on selectivity</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Batched Updates</strong=
>: Process multiple updates together to amortize overhead</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Automatic Cleanup</stro=
ng>: Remove old time buckets and perform maintenance automatically</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance-aware</stro=
ng>: Monitor update times and switch strategies if performance degrades</li=
>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance Characterist=
ics:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Index updates</strong>:=
 &lt; 5ms for batches of 100 transactions</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Query performance</stro=
ng>: 10-100x faster for selective filters</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory overhead</strong=
>: ~50 bytes per transaction for indices</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-time capability</s=
trong>: Can handle 1000+ updates/second without blocking UI</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This approach ensures that even =
with high-frequency updates, the filtering system maintains excellent perfo=
rmance while keeping indices fresh and accurate.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Br=
illiant! Your adaptive strategy selection and incremental indexing approach=
 shows deep understanding of real-world performance challenges. I'm particu=
larly impressed with how you balance accuracy with performance, and the aut=
omatic strategy switching based on filter selectivity.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me ask one final challenging=
 question: <strong>How would you handle the scenario where we need to imple=
ment cross-session state persistence for these filters and indices, conside=
ring that our fraud analysts often work in shifts and need to hand off thei=
r work to the next analyst? What are the trade-offs between different persi=
stence strategies?</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent question! <strong>Cross-session state persistence in financial applic=
ations is incredibly complex</strong> because you're balancing security, pe=
rformance, compliance, and user experience. In fraud detection, handoffs be=
tween analysts are critical - losing filter context or missing a flagged tr=
ansaction during shift changes could have serious consequences.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me design a <strong>multi-ti=
ered persistence strategy</strong> that addresses these challenges:</p>
